# SYNTHETIC electron-neutral momentum-transfer cross section.
#
# THIS IS NOT MEASURED DATA FOR NITROGEN OR ANY OTHER GAS.  It is an
# analytic model, written only so that in.table.electron runs out of the
# box and so that the shape exercises structure a VHS power law cannot
# represent: a Ramsauer-type minimum near 0.30 eV and a resonance peak
# near 2.30 eV.
#
#   sigma(E) = bg(E) [1 - 0.90 exp(-(ln(E/0.30)/1.10)^2)]
#              + 2.2e-19 exp(-(ln(E/2.30)/0.45)^2)
#   bg(E)    = 6e-20 [1 + 3/(1 + E/0.02)]
#
# To do real physics, replace this file with a genuine cross section from
# the LXCat project.  See the header of in.table.electron for how.
#
EN_RAMSAUER_DEMO
N 300 X energy XUNITS eV YUNITS m^2 EXTRAP constant powerlaw

